  STANDING DQs that apply to this instrument whatever it prints:
  1. The regexes are authored by machine 2. The NUMBER is derived; the CHOICE OF UNIT
     is declared. Matched lines are printed so the choice is disputable.
  2. D_sup counts FILES, not independent judgements. Three files by one machine on one
     evening are one judgement wearing three filenames. That is why the machine count
     is printed beside the file count and is the number to read.
  3. Token regexes are lexical. An item discussed without its token is invisible here,
     so D_sup is a LOWER BOUND on corroboration, never an upper bound.
  4. This census measures the RECORD, not the mathematics. An item with a large D_sup
     is well-discussed, not correct.
